INT. BOWLING ALLEY BASEMENT - ROLLER DERBY LOCKER ROOM - NIGHT

Cinderblock walls, a leaking pipe, the muffled thunder of strikes overhead. Benches bolted to the floor. A whiteboard reads "SEMIFINAL."

WANDA "WRECKER" PRUITT (30s, captain, stitches over one eyebrow) laces her skates. Beside her, DELPHINE ARCEMENT (20s, rookie jammer, wide-eyed) tapes her wrist guards.

SUNNY MAKOA (40s, blocker, built like a refrigerator) eats a banana. MARGUERITE VOSS (50s, coach, tracksuit, whistle) paces. GUS TREMAINE (60s, bout announcer, headset around his neck) leans in the doorway. TINY FOLAU (20s, pivot, five-foot-nothing, enormous voice) sits on a cooler.

MARGUERITE
Listen up. We are down two points in the standings and they have the best jammer in the league.

WANDA
Which is why we skate her into the wall, Coach.

DELPHINE
Wrecker, I thought we weren't allowed to plan that.

WANDA
Rookie, we're allowed to plan anything. We're just not allowed to get caught.

SUNNY
Wanda has a point. Also, the wall is very hard.

TINY
Sunny, you ate a whole banana in two bites. Respect.

SUNNY
Tiny, I am a professional.

GUS
Ladies, three minutes to first whistle. Somebody tell me how to pronounce "Delphine Arcement" for the crowd.

DELPHINE
Del-FEEN. Ar-suh-MAHN.

GUS
Del-FEEN Ar-suh-MAHN. Got it. And you, Tiny?

TINY
Tiny. Like the opposite of me.

GUS
It's poetry, kid.

MARGUERITE
Gus, out. Now.

GUS
Out. I'm out. Break a leg, but not really.

Gus exits.

WANDA
Rookie, you're jamming second period.

DELPHINE
Me? Wrecker, I've only done it in practice.

WANDA
Practice is where you stop being scared of the real thing.

DELPHINE
I am scared of the real thing.

SUNNY
Good. Scared people duck.

MARGUERITE
Delphine. Look at me. You skate the inside line. Sunny and Tiny open the gap. Wanda holds the pivot.

TINY
(shouting up the stairs)
Hey! Somebody shut off the pipe!

SUNNY
Tiny, it's a basement. There's always a pipe.

WANDA
Then we skate like there's no pipe.

A thunderous strike rolls overhead. A whistle blows upstairs.

WANDA (CONT'D)
(standing)
Hands in.

DELPHINE
Wait. Who says it?

WANDA
You do.

Delphine's hand is shaking. She puts it in anyway.

WANDA
(CONT'D)
Say it, Rookie.

TINY
Say it, Del-FEEN.

SUNNY
^Say it, kid.

DELPHINE
(barely)
On three.
